## Hardware Architecture

Universes
- Universe 1 (Serial1, Teensy pin 1 TX): 3 lamps in chain (A1, A2, A3).
- Universe 2 (Serial2, Teensy pin 8 TX): 2 lamps in chain (A4, A5).

Wiring (Teensy 4.1)
- Serial1 TX: pin 1 → RS‑485 DI on Shield #1 (Universe 1)
- Serial2 TX: pin 8 → RS‑485 DI on Shield #2 (Universe 2)
- Optional RX lines not used for send‑only DMX.
- GND: common between Teensy, shields, and lamp PSU
- XLR to lamps: Pin 1 GND, Pin 2 Data− (B), Pin 3 Data+ (A)
- Termination: last fixture in each chain ON (120 Ω)
- DE/RE on shields: tie to enable transmit (or follow shield docs). DMX is transmit‑only for controller.

Control UART (commands)
- Use a free UART on Teensy for external commands (e.g., Serial3). Wire RX/TX to your controller’s TX/RX per Teensy 4.1 pinout. Share GND.
- During development, the same commands can be sent over USB Serial.

Power
- Lamps powered from mains with their PSUs.
- Teensy powered via USB or regulated 5V; do not power lamps from Teensy.

